  "goodToKnow": "Kraus means frizzy or curly (krauses Haar), wrinkled (die Stirn kraus ziehen, to frown) and figuratively muddled: krause Ideen, krauses Zeug reden. Kräuseln means to ripple or curl: Das Wasser kräuselt sich. Der Krauskopf is someone with curly hair. Kraus is also a common German surname, and Krause even more so. Die Krause was a ruffled collar worn in the 16th century, like those in Renaissance portraits."
